%[text] ![Function Icon](text:image:7e81)**`LookAtNormalVector(str)`**
%[text] Explore the concept of normal unit vectors along the different control surfaces. The input string `str` refers to the right control surface `"CSR"`, the left control surface `"CSL"`, and the bottom control surface `"CSB"`..
%[text] **Example:**
%[text] ```matlabCodeExample
%[text] LookAtNormalVector("CSR")
%[text] ```
%[text] This code would draw Saturn V zoomed-in the bottom surface of the rocket with plotting of the exhaust velocity.


function LookAtNormalVector(str)
    arguments
        str (1,1) string {mustBeMember(str,["none" "CSR" "CSL" "CSB"])} = "none"
    end
    DrawSaturn(Highlight=str, NormalVector=true);
    title("Normal Unit Vector")
end
